  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical particles each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;go round a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;under the action of their mutual gravitational attraction. The angular speed of each particle will be :&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The gravitational force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mfenced></math> between the particles is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The centripetal force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of each particle can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Under balanced condition, equate equation (1) and equation (2) and simplify to obtain the angular speed of each particle.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
